# Waiver and Free Agency Events

## Purpose

This chapter defines the canonical events governing the acquisition of Players who are not currently owned by a Franchise.

Unlike Trades, which transfer ownership between Franchises, or Drafts, which introduce new Players into League competition, Waivers and Free Agency govern the redistribution of unowned Players.

These events ensure that every Player transitions through a deterministic ownership lifecycle while respecting League rules regarding waiver priority, claim windows, roster legality, contracts, and salary cap constraints.

---

# Guiding Principle

Released Players become League assets.

Waivers determine who earns acquisition rights.

Free Agency grants ownership when no competing claims exist.

Ownership begins only after successful acquisition.

---

# Acquisition Model

```text
Owned Player
      │
Player Released
      │
      ▼
Free Agent Pool
      │
      ├──────────────┐
      ▼              ▼
Waiver Claim     Direct Free Agent Signing
      │              │
      └──────┬───────┘
             ▼
Roster Assignment Created
             │
             ▼
Contract Created
```

Players are never "ownerless."

They exist in either:

- Franchise ownership
- League Free Agent Pool

---

# Acquisition Lifecycle

```text
PlayerReleased
        │
        ▼
PlayerAddedToWaivers
        │
        ▼
WaiverClaimSubmitted
        │
        ▼
WaiverClaimProcessed
        │
        ▼
WaiverClaimAwarded
        │
        ▼
RosterAssignmentCreated
        │
        ▼
ContractCreated
```

Alternative path:

```text
PlayerAvailableForFreeAgency
        │
        ▼
FreeAgentSigned
        │
        ▼
RosterAssignmentCreated
```

